 - A Chat upstream that wants a turn's reasoning back (`chatReplaysReasoning` in [`chat.go`](../../internal/gateway/chat.go): a host or a model, as magpie or the provider names it, with `deepseek` in it, such as OpenCode Go's `deepseek-v4.1-flash`, or Command Code's plugin) gets every assistant tool call with `reasoning_content`, relayed (`withReasoningOnToolTurns` in `passthrough`) or translated (`buildChat`). DeepSeek turns the whole request away ("The `reasoning_content` in the thinking mode must be passed back to the API") when a tool call made since the user's last message has none, which a client sends for a turn it saw no thinking on: another model's, a translated one (#1462). The turn's own thinking goes back as it came; one sent in `reasoning` or `reasoning_details` moves into `reasoning_content`, with those source fields removed (#3165). A relayed DeepSeek message carrying both `reasoning` and `reasoning_content`, including a non-tool message, keeps only `reasoning_content` (`foldReasoningAliases`); its serde reads the two names as one field and rejects duplicates. `TestChatToolTurnReasoningCarriedOnce` and `TestChatBothReasoningSpellingsRelayed` cover both cases; otherwise it goes with a space (`noReasoning`: DeepSeek's Chat API takes an empty one, but a relay that leaves empty fields out would drop it). An assistant message right after a tool result, a reply with no call of its own, gets one too: DeepSeek refuses it the same way (checked 2026-10-12, #1822). A reply with only one reasoning spelling, any other model and Mistral (#494) are sent as before.
